    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.forest_hills_queens"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Forest Hills is five subway stops and a world away from Manhattan. A few high-rises aside, the skyline is low and the houses are detached. Curved streets and Tudor-style buildings cover the neighborhoodâ€™s midsection, which is taken up by a planned community named Forest Hills Gardens. The commercial streets are modest and the community, which has a large population of European Jews, is family-oriented â€” a neighborhood best known as a place to settle and stay put.
