    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.west_village_manhattan"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Starving artists may not be able afford the West Village anymore, but this quaint neighborhood of 19th-century townhouses is still bohemian at heart. Old bookstores remain, voters are intensely liberal and cafes are packed with underemployed writers.
In recent years, the charming maze of historic homes and downtown edge has also attracted young families and well-heeled professionals alike. There's also a smattering of celebrities, long before Sex and the City turned a bakery into a tourist magnet.
Read More ...
To Do  |  Schools  |  Crime  |  Housing Stock  |  Who Lives There?  |  Walking Tour  |  Where Is It?</skos:definition>
